 "endReason": "escalated",
 "customerTurns": 3,
 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "We had a power cut last night and now our Candy washer dryer is completely dead - no lights, nothing. Everything else in the house came back on. The plug fuse is fine, I swapped it. Help!"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Since other appliances are working and the plug fuse is intact, the issue likely depends on whether power is actually reaching the machine's internal wiring or if the main control board has failed. You should verify that the socket is live using a separate tester to rule out a local circuit fault before assuming the appliance is broken. From what you have described, the most likely cause is property socket / supply / switched fused spur. Next: Check the socket works with another appliance and that any separate switched/fused spur controlling it is on (especially after a recent move). Let me know what you find."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Yes I already checked the socket - plugged a lamp into it and the lamp works fine. So the socket is live. Washer-dryer is still completely dead, even after unplugging it for over 10 minutes."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "From what you have described, the most likely cause is mains interference suppressor / mains filter. Next: Check the plug is fully seated and the lead undamaged - vibration can work a plug loose over time. Let me know what you find."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Plug looks fine and the cable isn't damaged. It's pushed fully into the socket too. Still completely dead though, so what next?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Since the power supply and cable are confirmed good, the issue likely lies with a blown internal thermal fuse or a failed main control board. You will need to remove the back panel to inspect these components for continuity, which requires disconnecting the appliance from the mains first. Next: If there was a pop/bang/burning smell, or any sign of burnt wiring, stop using it and unplug it. Let me know what you find."
  }
 ],
